  "notes": "Refers specifically to gaining financial profit. The emphasis is on the result of earning money rather than the labor involved. Often used in casual conversation about business success or investment gains.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{儲|もう}けている indicates a state of being profitable or currently earning money.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {株|かぶ}で{儲|もう}ける (make money on stocks)\n- {商売|しょうばい}で{儲|もう}ける (profit from business)\n- たくさん{儲|もう}ける (earn a lot)\n- ぼろ{儲|もう}け (making a killing, huge profit)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {稼|かせ}ぐ — to earn (emphasizes working to earn income, not just profit)\n- {設|もう}ける — homophone but means to establish or set up; written with a different kanji\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nIn Japanese culture, openly discussing how much one has profited can be seen as boastful. The expression {儲|もう}け{話|ばなし} (money-making scheme) often carries a slightly suspicious connotation.",
